From: Rajan Yadav <rajanyadav0307@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: sunxi: Unregister the extcon notifier in sunxi_musb_exit()

Unbinding/rebinding the musb-hdrc child fails with -EEXIST because the
devm extcon notifier registered on the glue device stays registered
across child unbinds. Use the non-devm extcon_register_notifier() and
unregister it in sunxi_musb_exit() (before cancel_work_sync()) and on
the init error path.

Fixes: bb1d1ce8c74e ("usb: musb: sunxi: Uses the resource-managed extcon API when registering extcon notifier")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Rajan Yadav <rajanyadav0307@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
@@ -279,15 +279,19 @@
 
 	writeb(SUNXI_MUSB_VEND0_PIO_MODE, musb->mregs + SUNXI_MUSB_VEND0);
 
-	/* Register notifier before calling phy_init() */
-	ret = devm_extcon_register_notifier(glue->dev, glue->extcon,
-					EXTCON_USB_HOST, &glue->host_nb);
+	/*
+	 * Register notifier before calling phy_init(). It is unregistered in
+	 * sunxi_musb_exit(), as this runs again each time the musb-hdrc child
+	 * is bound.
+	 */
+	ret = extcon_register_notifier(glue->extcon, EXTCON_USB_HOST,
+				       &glue->host_nb);
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_reset_assert;
 
 	ret = phy_init(glue->phy);
 	if (ret)
-		goto error_reset_assert;
+		goto error_unregister_notifier;
 
 	musb->isr = sunxi_musb_interrupt;
 
@@ -296,6 +300,9 @@
 
 	return 0;
 
+error_unregister_notifier:
+	extcon_unregister_notifier(glue->extcon, EXTCON_USB_HOST,
+				   &glue->host_nb);
 error_reset_assert:
 	if (test_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_HAS_RESET, &glue->flags))
 		reset_control_assert(glue->rst);
@@ -313,6 +320,9 @@
 
 	pm_runtime_put(musb->controller);
 
+	/* Before cancel_work_sync(), so the notifier cannot requeue the work */
+	extcon_unregister_notifier(glue->extcon, EXTCON_USB_HOST,
+				   &glue->host_nb);
 	cancel_work_sync(&glue->work);
 	if (test_bit(SUNXI_MUSB_FL_PHY_ON, &glue->flags))
 		phy_power_off(glue->phy);
